<header class="command-bar">
  <h1 data-i18n="title">ETF Momentum</h1>
  <div class="segment-toggle" role="tablist" aria-label="Dashboard segment">
    {% if active_segment == "sectors" %}
    <span class="segment-btn active" aria-current="page" data-i18n="segment_sectors">Themes</span>
    {% else %}
    <a class="segment-btn" href="index.html" data-i18n="segment_sectors">Themes</a>
    {% endif %}
    {#- The experimental badge sits OUTSIDE the [data-i18n] span on purpose: applyLang()
        rewrites that node's textContent, so a badge nested inside it would be
        wiped on the first language switch. -#}
    {% if active_segment == "sentiment" %}
    <span class="segment-btn active" aria-current="page"><span data-i18n="segment_sentiment">Sentiment</span><span class="experimental-badge" data-i18n="badge_experimental">experimental</span></span>
    {% else %}
    <a class="segment-btn" href="sentiment.html"><span data-i18n="segment_sentiment">Sentiment</span><span class="experimental-badge" data-i18n="badge_experimental">experimental</span></a>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="meta-cluster">
    {#- The scan-date block below exists only on pages sharing this header
        without their own summary strip — today that is the Sentiment page
        (code review, 2026-08-23: the guard used to be duplicated on the
        conditional inside the block, which a future third segment could
        silently opt into by half-editing; it is now checked once here
        instead). The auth block that follows is a sibling, not nested here —
        it renders on every segment, guarded only by `auth`. -#}
    {% if active_segment != "sectors" %}
    {#- index.html.j2's summary strip prints the scan id/date on desktop via
        .strip-subline; sentiment.html.j2 has no strip of its own, so without
        this row the Sentiment page showed no scan date anywhere on desktop
        once data WAS present — the 2026-08-22 fix only covered the empty
        state. Own condition (scan_date alone): a build with no auth
        configured still has a scan to name. Hidden at/below 600px —
        .mobile-scan-meta already covers the row there (see
        _responsive.css.j2's paired boundary). -#}
    {% if scan_date %}
    <span class="desktop-scan-meta">
      <span data-i18n="scan_prefix">Scan</span> #{{ active_scan_id }}
      <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> {{ scan_date[:10] }}
    </span>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if auth %}
    <span class="auth-root" id="auth-root">
      <button id="auth-signin" class="lang-toggle" type="button" data-i18n="auth_sign_in">Sign in</button>
      <form id="auth-form" class="auth-form" hidden>
        <input id="auth-email" class="auth-email" type="email" required autocomplete="email"
               placeholder="you@example.com" aria-label="Email">
        <button id="auth-send" class="lang-toggle auth-send" type="submit" data-i18n="auth_send_link">Send link</button>
        <span id="auth-status" class="auth-status" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </form>
      <span id="auth-user" hidden>
        <span id="auth-email-label" class="scan-meta"></span>
        <button id="auth-signout" class="lang-toggle" type="button" data-i18n="auth_sign_out">Sign out</button>
      </span>
    </span>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="theme-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Colour theme">
      <button type="button" class="theme-btn" data-theme-choice="auto" aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Auto" data-i18n="theme_auto">Auto</button>
      <button type="button" class="theme-btn" data-theme-choice="light" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Light" data-i18n="theme_light">☀</button>
      <button type="button" class="theme-btn" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Dark" data-i18n="theme_dark">☾</button>
    </div>
    <button id="lang-toggle" class="lang-toggle" type="button" onclick="toggleLang()" aria-label="Switch language">SV</button>
  </div>
  {#- Mobile-only second row: the meta-cluster's scan context condenses to
      icon-only/hidden below 600px (see _responsive.css.j2's touch-target
      rules), so a phone reader loses the scan id and date entirely. This
      mirrors them in one condensed line. Named .mobile-scan-meta, not
      .scan-meta: that class already exists on #auth-email-label above (the
      signed-in user's email) — an unrelated element this would silently
      collide with if reused. Visibility is entirely _responsive.css.j2's
      call (display:none there above 600px), not an inline style — that
      file is guaranteed last in the cascade (see its own header comment)
      so nothing here needs to pre-hide it.

      Guarded on scan_date, not just wrapped: `scan_date[:10]` slices an
      undefined var, which raises (Jinja's default Undefined tolerates bare
      `{{ }}` output but not slicing) rather than rendering blank — hit by
      tests/test_leaderboard_filters.py's minimal render context, which
      passes no scan_date at all. -#}
  {% if scan_date %}
  <div class="mobile-scan-meta">
    <span data-i18n="scan_prefix">Scan</span> #{{ active_scan_id }}
    <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> {{ scan_date[:10] }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</header>